--- Path reconciliation (no silent drift; Honesty Covenant #7 no predecessor bypass) ---
The generated prompt names the output `apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Battery/SleepEfficiencyPage.xaml`
+ `SleepEfficiencyPageViewModel.cs`. That project/folder does NOT exist in this repo. Every
gate-passing W7 predecessor (page:driving/RegenEfficiency, page:battery/BatteryDegradation,
page:battery/ProjectedRange, page:battery/EnergyProducts, …) lives in project `TeslaSync.App` under
`feature-views/<Page>/` as a code-only WinUI 3 `UserControl` (no XAML markup file), split into
<Page>.cs (view) + .Model.cs + .Source.cs + .ViewModel.cs. The pure-C# Model/Source/ViewModel are
linked into TeslaSync.App.Tests for headless verification and the view is registered in the
NavigationView via ShellWindow.xaml.cs PageFactory.Register. This unit follows that identical,
accepted structure rather than the templated path — the "native WinUI 3 / Fluent" implementation in
this repo is code-built UserControls + design tokens, not XAML markup.

