--- Data source bound to the generated C# client (P1/S8 ObservableObject-style ViewModel) ---
useSleepEfficiency   GET /analytics/sleep [vehicle_id, days, start, end]
  -> SleepEfficiencyClientFeed.FetchAsync  (operation get_api_v1_analytics_sleep,
     Operations.Analytics.Sleep; web hook web/src/api/hooks/useEnergy.ts useSleepEfficiency).
  Query shaping mirrors the web hook verbatim: vehicle_id + days (default 30); start/end appended
  ONLY when both bounds are present (web L142-143). Raw JSON round-trips through the tolerant
  SleepEfficiencySummary.FromJson (snake_case wire shape; camelCase alias also accepted). A failed
  read propagates the client ApiException to the error surface; a non-object body composes the empty
  snapshot (web `sleep` undefined -> empty surface). The production parameterless ctor binds the
  EmptySleepEfficiencyFeed (the accepted predecessor seam; the wired client feed is unit-tested and
  ready for DI), identical to RegenEfficiencyPage/BatteryDegradationPage.

--- SI / units at the display boundary (P1/S5) ---
The /analytics/sleep scalars are display-shaped/dimensionless (percent, %/hour, currency, kWh,
minutes); the only SI quantity is each event's outside temperature (SI Celsius), converted with
UnitConverters.TemperatureFromSi + UnitLabels.Label(pref.Temperature) at the render boundary only
(SleepEfficiencyProjection.BuildTable). No non-SI value is stored or computed.

--- Architecture ---
View (SleepEfficiencyPage.cs) is a thin renderer over SleepEfficiencyDisplay; all branch selection,
formatting and i18n live in the WinUI-free SleepEfficiencyProjection.Project. State marshalled to the
UI thread via DispatcherQueue. Fluent components only (TsStatCard, TsChartContainer, TsPieChart,
TsBarChart, TsGlassPanel, TsDataTable, TsEmptyState, TsQueryError, TsDataFreshness, TsFadeIn,
PageTitle/Subhead/SectionTitle/PanelTitle/Caption) + design tokens (DisplayTokens / ChartBrushes /
StatusResources) — no inline colors/typography, no web pixel-cloning, no direct recharts/leaflet.

