Note on extra resolved keys: SleepStrings also resolves sleep.error (error-surface title) and
common.retry (retry affordance) beyond the 32 manifest strings — both follow the web page's
ErrorDisplay/QueryError affordances and the predecessor RegenEfficiency pattern. They are NOT counted
toward PARITY_REQUIRED/PARITY_COVERED.

Note on state labels: the web STATE_LABELS / STATE_COLORS maps (Sleeping / Online-Idle / Driving /
Charging / Updating / Suspended) are plain data labels the web hardcodes (never run through t()); the
native port mirrors them verbatim in SleepEfficiencyProjection.StateLabel/StateColorIndex for donut
parity. Donut wedge + legend chip share one brand palette index (ChartBrushes.ForIndex) per state.

a11y: AutomationProperties.SetName on the page, every metric TsStatCard, the donut, the comparison
chart, each legend chip, the impact-callout stats and the drain-events table; the empty/error
surfaces announce via live regions; Fluent components carry built-in keyboard/pointer + light/dark via
design tokens — no hardcoded colors/typography.

